## TIẾNG ANH · 16:30–17:00 — Thứ Ba: Giải thích khái niệm

### 16:30–16:40 · Shadowing

2 phút video Callstack. Nghe → dừng → nhại to.

### 16:40–16:55 · Nói to có ghi âm

**Chủ đề: TurboModules khác native module cũ chỗ nào.**

> *"There are two differences that actually matter in practice.*
> *The first is lazy loading. Under the old system, every native module was instantiated when the app started, whether you used it or not. So an app with thirty modules paid the startup cost for all thirty. TurboModules are only created the first time JavaScript reaches for them. I verified this in my own app — I put a log in the constructor, launched the app, and nothing fired until I opened the screen that uses the module.*
> *The second is type safety. You write a TypeScript spec, and Codegen generates the native interfaces from it. So if the Kotlin signature doesn't match the spec, it fails at compile time. In the old architecture you wrote the JavaScript side and the native side separately and kept them in sync by hand — mismatches showed up as runtime crashes.*
> *The trade-off is that synchronous calls are now possible, which is genuinely useful for things like reading a layout measurement. But they run on the JavaScript thread, so anything slow in a synchronous method freezes the UI. It's a sharper tool."*

### 16:55–17:00 · 5 từ mới

| Từ / cụm | Nghĩa | Câu mẫu |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `reach for` | với tới, gọi tới | *The first time JavaScript reaches for it.* |
| `fire` (v) | được kích hoạt | *Nothing fired until I opened that screen.* |
| `mismatch` (n) | sự lệch nhau | *Mismatches showed up as runtime crashes.* |
| `freeze` (v) | đứng hình | *A slow sync method freezes the UI.* |
| `a sharper tool` | công cụ sắc hơn (mạnh nhưng dễ đứt tay) | *It's a sharper tool.* |

